Help for JUPE:

JUPE introduces a fake server with the given name, so
that the real server cannot connect.

Jupes are stored in the services database. They are
reintroduced when services restarts or relinks, when
the jupe is removed with /squit, and when a real server
with that name links. Use JUPE DEL to remove a jupe.

JUPE <server> <reason> is the same as JUPE ADD.

Syntax: JUPE ADD <server> <reason>
Syntax: JUPE DEL <server>
Syntax: JUPE LIST [mask]
Syntax: JUPE SYNC

JUPE ADD on an existing jupe updates its reason.
JUPE SYNC reintroduces every jupe on the network.

Examples:
    /msg &nick& JUPE ADD irc.blah.net very unstable server
    /msg &nick& JUPE DEL irc.blah.net
    /msg &nick& JUPE LIST *.blah.net
